<div class="container">
  <img class="brand-mascot" src={~p"/images/brand/mascot.png"} alt="Popcorn mascot with a laptop" />
  <p>Make your terminal sessions pop.</p>
  <h2>About {@server_name}</h2>

  <p>
    <strong>{@server_name}</strong>
    is a platform for hosting and sharing
    terminal session recordings, powered by
    <%= if @server_version do %>
      <a href="https://docs.popcorn.local/manual/server/">popcorn server</a> ({@server_version}).
    <% else %>
      <a href="https://docs.popcorn.local/manual/server/">popcorn server</a>.
    <% end %>
  </p>

  <%= if @contact_email_address do %>
    <h2>{@server_name} admin contact</h2>

    <p>
      You can reach the administrator of this server at <strong><.obfuscated_email address={
          @contact_email_address
        } /></strong>.
    </p>

    <p>
      Consider contacting the admin in the following cases:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>account access problems,</li>
      <li>recording recovery,</li>
      <li>content reporting,</li>
      <li>security vulnerability, which may affect {@server_name} users.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      For other topics, check popcorn's <a href="https://docs.popcorn.local/faq/">FAQ</a>, or reach out to the <a href="https://docs.popcorn.local/community/">popcorn community</a>.
    </p>
  <% end %>

  <h2>About popcorn</h2>

  <p>
    <strong>popcorn</strong>
    is a suite of tools
    for recording, replaying, and sharing terminal sessions, maintained by smeltery.
    It builds on the open-source work of <a href="https://hachyderm.io/@ku1ik">Marcin Kulik</a>
    and the asciinema contributors.
  </p>

  <p>
    To learn more about the project, check out the documentation at <a href="https://docs.popcorn.local">docs.popcorn.local</a>.
    There you can find information on how popcorn works, how to engage with the community,
    what integrations people have built around the project, how to self-host your own popcorn server, and last but not least, how to support the project.
  </p>
</div>
